<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bagnolo in Piano</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bagnolo in Piano is a small town in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reggio-emilia">Reggio Emilia</a>, in the plain north of Reggio. From the 14th century it belonged, with Novellara, to a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga family</a>, who held both as imperial fiefs until their line died out in 1728. The territory later passed to the Este dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bagnolo-in-piano.jpg" alt="Bagnolo in Piano" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bucaramango · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Torrazzo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
